==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sol Dae Rokker CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
SOL DAE ROKKER's most noteworthy aspect is its multi-hit. Having a total of 400 standing range, its first hit spans up to 450 range. However, each added hit has less range than its base hit, and while that could be used to punish enemies that get too close to it, there are a handful of problems with the execution.

The first issue is that it DPS is nowhere near as impressive as it may first seem. As its first hit only produces 3k DPS, a very low amount for a unit of such range, and while this becomes 12k against his variety of targets, this is a lot lower than most other nukers. While he holds 6k at his 300 range hit, which is a more justifiable number, trying to get enemies into its range is a risky strategy. The second issue is its third hit, which only has a range of 1. On nearly every single scenario, SOL DAE ROKKER only has 2 hits, meaning its overall DPS is only 2/3 of the overall number. While it gets a lot of backwards piercing from its omni-strike, it's not an anti-zombie, so this usage only goes as far as a select few stages where a starred alien can warp it further down a stage, such as with [[Gardeneel Bros.|Gardeneel Bros]].

SOL DAE ROKKER shines on stages where you can easily get units into its inner range without it getting hit, and there's luckily a variety of low ranged enemies in all 3 traits. However, since its second hit will have a hard time hitting things that outrange it, make sure you have a way with dealing with these threats beforehand, as it first hit won't do that much damage.

While it has Colossus Slayer and features all the targets for [[Baron Seal Strikes]], its second hit can't outrange a lot of the threats on the stage. Luckily, its first hit has more acceptable damage against [[Baron Seal]] himself, and it can tank a bit, so its usage there isn't entirely discouraged.

